{"bug":"K001","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"2. Mixing infallible and unit-error loaders can panic","evidence":"“the infallible loader receives that error and reaches `unreachable!()`” describes concurrent mixed loaders, not a completed failed try_get_with whose retained error prevents a sequential initializer from running."}
{"bug":"K002","report":"B","v":"found","ref":"1. Async compute operations can lose updates.","evidence":"“releases the key’s compute lock before the requested insertion or removal finishes” identifies premature release in and_compute_with. “Actual results are `1, 2, 2`, leaving `2`” connects another computation reading stale data to a lost update."}
{"bug":"K004","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"5. Generation wrap prevents maintenance from cleaning up hot entries","evidence":"“the entry remains marked dirty after its write operations have been processed” concerns generation wrap. No finding identifies a queued Upsert re-admitting a removed entry and leaving an unreachable deque node that stalls eviction or leaks capacity."}
{"bug":"K005","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"Report-wide; closest capacity discussion is finding 5","evidence":"“Frequently updated entries retain invalidated values and consume capacity after maintenance” concerns generation wrap. The report does not identify a zero-capacity sync cache allowing an ordinary inserted value to be retrieved before maintenance."}
